**DISCHARGE DIAGNOSES**
\- {{ALL discharge diagnoses together in ONE combined list — one '\- ' dash line per diagnosis, the debility/rehabilitation diagnosis FIRST, then the rest; NO 'Principal'/'Active' sub-labels; each diagnosis maximally specific with ' [POA]' when present on SNF admission; include ALL supported diagnoses, omit none}}

**REASON FOR SNF ADMISSION / SNF COURSE NARRATIVE**
{{Provider-voice narrative per SNF_DISCHARGE_NARRATIVE_LOCK: open with 'In brief, [Patient Name] is a very pleasant [age] [sex] admitted to the SNF on [date] for skilled rehabilitation following [qualifying reason].' then summarize the qualifying hospitalization background, the SNF stay (therapy participation and functional progression with provided measures, medical events and management, named consultants when provided), and that rehabilitation goals were met or the provided reason for discharge. Use only provided data; no invented details; no source attribution.}}
The patient was evaluated on the day of discharge, and significant findings included {{day-of-discharge findings from provided data}}.
**Most recent vitals:** {{discharge-day vitals exactly as provided; if not provided write exactly: Please see PCC}}

**PHYSICAL EXAM**
{{Discharge-day exam. Never a paragraph: each system on its own line beginning with the literal three characters '\- ' (backslash, hyphen, space) — the backslash keeps the hyphen from rendering as a '•' bullet glyph. Use provided findings verbatim; generate a normal discharge baseline for any missing system; never write 'not provided'.}}
\- Gen: {{exam_general}}
\- HEENT: {{exam_heent}}
\- Resp: {{exam_resp}}
\- Cardio: {{exam_cardio}}
\- Abd: {{exam_abd}}
\- Ext: {{exam_ext}}
\- Neuro: {{exam_neuro}}
\- Psych: {{exam_psych}}

**SNF COURSE BY PROBLEM**

{{FORMAT (HARDWIRED): one block per Discharge Diagnoses entry, SAME order, debility/rehabilitation problem FIRST. Each block is EXACTLY: one BOLD title line — the literal character '#' immediately followed by the diagnosis with NO space after '#', bolded with '**' only, no heading marks — then, on the IMMEDIATELY following line with NO blank line in between, the dash lines: each item on its own line starting with the literal three characters '\- ' (backslash, hyphen, space). Never begin an item with unescaped '- ', '•', '*', numbered lists, or indentation. No blank lines between dash lines within a problem; exactly ONE blank line between problems. Evidence/course items first (SNF-stay facts, therapy findings, labs with exact values and dates as provided), then discharge actions (continued meds with dose/route/frequency exactly as provided — generic names only; post-discharge monitoring; follow-up). Minimum 4 dash lines per problem when data supports them. NO 'If X, then Y' advisory lines unless explicitly provided. The FIRST problem MUST follow SNF_DISCHARGE_DEBILITY_FIRST_LOCK and end with the standing line VERBATIM: '\- Discharge plan, medications, and follow-up reviewed with the patient/caregiver and nursing staff.'}}

{{FORMAT & DEPTH EXAMPLE — BEGIN. This block defines the REQUIRED structure and depth for EVERY problem block. It is a formatting example ONLY. NEVER copy its diagnoses, values, medications, dates, or therapy findings into the note; all real content comes exclusively from the provided input data.

**#Severe debility with generalized muscle weakness following hospitalization for community-acquired pneumonia, status post completed skilled rehabilitation, improved [POA]**
\- Admitted to the SNF 07/02 for skilled rehabilitation following hospitalization 06/20 through 07/01 for community-acquired pneumonia with deconditioning.
\- Admission PT evaluation: ambulated 40 feet with front-wheeled walker and contact-guard assist; required minimal assistance with ADLs.
\- Discharge PT evaluation (07/28): ambulates 250 feet with front-wheeled walker independently; independent with ADLs using adaptive equipment.
\- Participated in PT/OT five days weekly with good effort and steady progression; rehabilitation goals met.
\- Continue home exercise program and home physical therapy through the arranged home health services.
\- Discharge plan, medications, and follow-up reviewed with the patient/caregiver and nursing staff.

**#Hypertension [POA]**
\- Blood pressure remained controlled during the SNF stay, most recently 128/76.
\- Continued amlodipine 5 mg PO daily without change.
\- Continue amlodipine 5 mg PO daily after discharge.
\- Blood pressure monitoring by home health with PCP follow-up.

FORMAT & DEPTH EXAMPLE — END. Every real problem block below MUST match this structure and depth. This example governs ONLY the SNF COURSE BY PROBLEM section — every other section MUST still be rendered in full per FULL_NOTE_ALL_SECTIONS_REQUIRED_LOCK.}}

**#[Debility/Rehabilitation Dx Title per SNF_DISCHARGE_DEBILITY_FIRST_LOCK] [POA]**
\- {{course/evidence dash lines: qualifying stay and reason; ADMISSION vs DISCHARGE functional measures as provided; therapy participation.}}
\- {{discharge-action dash lines: home therapy plan through the arranged services; then the standing line VERBATIM: '\- Discharge plan, medications, and follow-up reviewed with the patient/caregiver and nursing staff.'}}

{{Repeat a problem block for ALL remaining discharge diagnoses, exactly ONE blank line between blocks.}}

**FUNCTIONAL STATUS AT DISCHARGE**
\- {{per FUNCTIONAL_PROGRESS_LOCK: ambulation (distance/device/assist) at discharge vs admission; transfers; ADLs; stairs, swallowing/diet per SLP when provided; recommended home therapy plan. If no therapy documentation provided: '\- See PT/OT discharge documentation in PCC.'}}

**DISCHARGE MEDICATIONS**
\- {{per SNF_DISCHARGE_MEDS_LOCK: one medication per '\- ' dash line, generic names only, dose/route/frequency exactly as provided; bold '**New:**'/'**Changed:**'/'**Continued:**'/'**Stopped:**' sub-labels only when the provided data distinguishes them; if none provided: '[See discharge medication reconciliation in PCC]'}}

**DISCHARGE CONDITION:** {{discharge_condition; if not provided write: Stable}}

**DISCHARGE DISPOSITION & SERVICES**
\- {{per SNF_DISCHARGE_DISPOSITION_SERVICES_LOCK: destination (typically home) and the arranged services EXACTLY as provided — home health (agency/disciplines/frequency when provided), Care Plus, HIHR (High Intensity Home Rehab), DME, caregiver support, transport; never invent a service; if nothing provided: '\- Not provided.'}}

**PENDING ITEMS FOR FOLLOW-UP:**
\- {{each pending lab/study/item on its own dash line with responsible party when provided; if none: '\- None.'}}

**FOLLOW-UP:**
\- {{follow-up providers/appointments/timeframes from provided data; if none provided: '\- Patient counseled to follow up with primary care provider within one week of discharge.'}}

**Code Status:** {{code_status — omit this entire line if not provided}}

